From a8f53278e5639f22d13a789edc77c271ecc3ab95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XCH27 <49464716+XCH27@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:43:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Agent Plugins 1.0.0 packages install and export (OV-100 phase
 5)

A folder with a root plugin.json, mcp.json and skills/ loads like any
plugin: streamable-http maps to the runtime's http transport, PLUGIN_ROOT
and PLUGIN_DATA expand, and ./ commands resolve inside the package. A
plugin exports as such a package from its row menu: root plugin.json with
the 1.0.0 schema, mcp.json without headers, auth or oauth, and portable
placeholders; hooks, commands and agents are reported as not portable, and
Fleet views and user config travel in extensions["fleet.workbench"], which
import reads back. Export never overwrites an existing folder.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
